; F5b (friction-cn): P0 process/adverse fault matrix. Drives the compiled
; c2c binary as a SUBPROCESS against the F5a scripted fault server
; (Relay_test_support): relay register / dm send / dm poll / status vs
; 401/429/5xx, truncated + malformed JSON, connection refused, empty
; response, client timeout; PoW adverse challenges (garbage/wrong-ctx/
; accept-then-401/endless) pinning the single-minted-retry bound; doctor
; --relay exit contract vs a refused relay; and the strict B098 vector
; (relay-delivered verdict -> real `relay connect --once` -> inert at
; `await-reply`; host-local verdict file still resolves). Two known
; defects are documented as skipped FIXME cases (5xx ok:true false
; success; doctor relay.reachable false PASS). Appended LAST per the
; serialized manifest-lane discipline (H4->J1->H5->H6->F5a->F5b).
